{#
  Who the page in front of the reader is by: the `p-author h-card` the source
  design puts in an entry's footer (decision-16, TASK-83).

  It replaces `partials/byline.njk`, which printed a name in a meta line. This
  is the whole credit — a round photo, "Written by" linked to their archive
  with `rel="author me"`, what they do, where they are, what they wrote about
  themselves and the links they call their own.

  The person and only the person (TASK-105). The site menu used to be printed
  here as well, because the design had no header navigation; it is in
  `header.global-header` on every page now, so this card says nothing about
  the site and a reader looking for the way around never has to find the bio
  first.

  Set `bioAuthor` before including it and nothing renders when that is absent:

    {% set bioAuthor = author %}
    {% include "partials/bio.njk" %}

  `bioAuthor` is one of the profile objects the context carries — `author` on a
  post, `siteAuthor` on a page, the archive's person on an author archive — so
  what a reader sees and what `partials/jsonld.njk` says come from one record
  and cannot drift. Every field but `name` is optional: a profile with nothing
  in it prints a name and nothing else, and a name this site has no account for
  is printed unlinked, because the file still said somebody wrote this.

  `bioLead` is what the line opens with, "Written by" unless a layout says
  otherwise. An author archive sets "Posts by", because the card there heads a
  list of somebody's writing rather than crediting one piece of it.

  A link's `rel` always holds `me` — the CMS puts it there whether or not the
  Links box typed it — followed by whatever else that line carried, so this
  prints one attribute rather than one of its own beside one of theirs.

  The `p-note` and the `rel="me"` links are printed wherever the card is, which
  is what `bioProfile` used to ask for on an author archive alone. An entry
  left that switch unset because the page footer carried the site's identity
  links; it carries nobody's now, so somebody's links belong under what they
  wrote rather than one page further on.
#}
{% if bioAuthor %}
<div class="bio p-author h-card">
  {%- if bioAuthor.avatar %}
  <div class="bio-avatar">
    <img class="u-photo" src="{{ bioAuthor.avatar | url }}" alt="{{ bioAuthor.name }}" width="50" height="50">
  </div>
  {%- endif %}

  <div>
    <p>
      {{ bioLead | default("Written by") }}
      {%- if bioAuthor.url %}
      <a class="u-url p-name" rel="author me" href="{{ bioAuthor.url | url }}">{{ bioAuthor.name }}</a>
      {%- else %}
      <strong class="p-name">{{ bioAuthor.name }}</strong>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- if bioAuthor.jobTitle %}, a <span class="p-job-title">{{ bioAuthor.jobTitle }}</span>{% endif %}
      {%- if bioAuthor.location %} from <span class="p-locality">{{ bioAuthor.location }}</span>{% endif %}.
    </p>

    {%- if bioAuthor.bio %}
    <p class="bio-note p-note">{{ bioAuthor.bio }}</p>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- if bioAuthor.links.length %}
    <ul class="hlist bio-links">
      {%- for link in bioAuthor.links %}
      <li><a class="u-url" rel="{{ link.rel }}" href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.label }}</a></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
